Usage: simulate-workflow <workflow-file> [event-type] [event-payload-json-file] [--json]

Dry-runs a whole workflow locally with act (default event: push). Without a payload file a minimal
payload for the event is written to a temporary file and removed on exit. Without act, the docker
CLI or a reachable Docker daemon the run is skipped with exit 0. --json prints {ok, data, findings}
on stdout.
Exit codes: 0 ok or skipped, 1 file not found, otherwise the status of act, 2 usage error.
